node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
_reference/
.cts-cache/

# Wrangler local dev state. Never track this: cf.json caches the geolocation of
# whatever connection last ran wrangler (city, postcode, lat/long, ISP), and
# wrangler-account.json holds the Cloudflare account id and account name.
.wrangler/

# Private working notes — never commit these (market position, other repos, account details).
NOTES.private.md
marketing.html

# `npm pack` output — the release workflow builds one as a Release asset.
*.tgz

# `npm run bundle` output — built in CI, attached to the release.
standalone/

# `npx skills` manager state. The skill itself is tracked in .claude/skills/.
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Fetched from the GitHub Release at deploy time by deploy-site.yml — never committed.
site/public/cleartoship.mjs
site/public/cleartoship-standalone.tgz
site/public/SHA256SUMS

# Claude Code agent worktrees (local only)
.claude/worktrees/

# The key to the anonymised app labels in this repo's notes — never commit (this repo is public)
.feedback-key.md

# bugdetect audit handoff (/Users/Shared/bugdetector). AUDIT-BRIEF.md lists the
# file and line of every UNFIXED finding here, and this repo is public — that is
# a map for anyone hostile, worth more than the findings are. The notices it
# drops in the root quote other, PRIVATE apps by name, which the rule at the top
# of CLAUDE.md forbids writing down here at all.
#
# AUDIT-REPLY.json is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the decision trail, it is
# meant to be committed, and it holds only this repo's own paths plus the reasons
# — read it before each commit and keep another app's name out of it.
AUDIT-BRIEF.md
BUGDETECT-NOTICE.md
